1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,050
The fastest way to stall your

2
00:00:02,050 --> 00:00:04,596
momentum in a fast-changing world is

3
00:00:04,596 --> 00:00:07,353
locking yourself into a rigid five-year

4
00:00:07,353 --> 00:00:08,060
life plan.

5
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:11,051
Neuroscientist Anne-Laure Le Cunff wrote about

6
00:00:11,051 --> 00:00:13,587
why ambitious planners burn out chasing

7
00:00:13,587 --> 00:00:14,497
fixed ladders.

8
00:00:14,497 --> 00:00:16,383
In her book Tiny Experiments,

9
00:00:16,383 --> 00:00:18,399
she argues that we learn faster

10
00:00:18,399 --> 00:00:20,675
from short feedback loops than from

11
00:00:20,675 --> 00:00:22,040
distant finish lines.

12
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:24,601
A massive five-year goal frames every

13
00:00:24,601 --> 00:00:26,470
